  "database": "rschema_0448",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0448 database is designed to manage various aspects of a laboratory setting, including user information, equipment, consumables, hazardous chemicals, and course participation. The User table stores information about each user, including their associated unit, password, phone number, role, username, and a unique identifier. The Experimental_Equipment table contains details about the laboratory equipment, such as its acquisition time, category, device ID, model, name, manufacturer, and status. The Experimental_Consumables table tracks consumables, including their category, ID, name, inventory quantity, and status. Hazardous_Chemicals stores information about hazardous chemicals, including their ID, name, inventory quantity, issuance time, and status. The Experimental_Course table manages course information, including the class location, time, ID, name, participants, and the ID of the teacher who teaches the course. The User_Usage_of_Equipment table records when a user uses a piece of equipment, including the device ID, usage purpose, usage time, and the user's ID. The User_Purchase_Consumables table tracks when a user purchases consumables, including the consumable ID, purchase time, and the user's ID. Similarly, the User_Purchase_Hazardous_Chemicals table records when a user purchases hazardous chemicals, including the chemical ID, purchase time, and the user's ID. The User_Participation_in_Course table tracks a user's participation in a course, including the course ID, grade, participation status, and the user's ID. Each of these tables is linked to the User table through foreign keys, which establish relationships between users and the various laboratory resources they interact with.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\n1.User Management:\nManage user information, including user roles (Student, Teacher, Laboratory Administrator, Experimental Center Director Administrator, System Administrator), username, password, phone number, and associated unit.\n2.Experimental Equipment Management:\nEnter and manage the basic information of laboratory equipment, such as equipment name, model, category, manufacturer, status (inactive, in use, active), and acquisition time.\nUsage Records Management: Record the usage of equipment, including usage time, user, and purpose of use.\nCourse Association Management: Associate equipment with specific experimental courses for easier scheduling and management of the equipment.\n3.Laboratory Consumables Management:\nConsumables Management: Perform operations such as archiving, modifying, and querying consumables information. Manage the purchasing, storage, issuance, and return of consumables.\nRecord consumable name, category, inventory quantity, and status. Users can purchase consumables and record the purchase time.\n4.Hazardous Chemicals Management:\nArchive, modify, and query hazardous chemicals information. Manage the purchasing, storage, issuance, and return of hazardous chemicals to ensure safety.\nRecord chemical name, inventory quantity, issuance time, and status.\n5.Experimental Course Management:\nView and manage information for regular experimental courses, including course name, class time, and class location. Each course can have multiple students registered, and each course is assigned a corresponding teacher.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0448.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0448\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `unit` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `experimental_equipment` (\n  `equipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `model` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `manufacturer` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `acquisition_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`equipment_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `experimental_consumables` (\n  `consumable_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `inventory_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`consumable_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `hazardous_chemicals` (\n  `chemical_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `inventory_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `issuance_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`chemical_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `experimental_course` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `class_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `participants` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `teacher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`teacher_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_usage_of_equipment` (\n  `usage_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `usage_purpose` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `usage_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`usage_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `usage_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `usage_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `experimental_equipment` (`device_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_purchase_consumables` (\n  `purchase_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `consumable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`purchase_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_consumables_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_consumables_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`consumable_id`) REFERENCES `experimental_consumables` (`consumable_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_purchase_hazardous_chemicals` (\n  `purchase_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `chemical_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`purchase_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_hazardous_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_hazardous_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`chemical_id`) REFERENCES `hazardous_chemicals` (`chemical_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_participation_in_course` (\n  `participation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `grade` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `participation_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`participation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `participation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `participation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `experimental_course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
